            "KB-006"
          ],
          "confidence": "high",
          "replyMarkdown": "Sorry about the dropped VPN connection, especially during calls — that's frustrating. Here are some steps to try, in order:\n\n1. **Check your home internet first**: open a public website without the VPN connected. If it's slow or drops too, restart your router and try again.\n2. **If you're on Wi-Fi**, move closer to the router, or better yet, connect via an Ethernet cable. A weak Wi-Fi signal is the most common cause of this issue.\n3. **Fully disconnect the VPN**, close the VPN client completely, then reopen it and reconnect.\n4. **Turn off any other VPN or security tool** running on your laptop — two of them competing for the network connection can cause drops.\n5. **Restart your laptop**, then connect to the VPN before opening any other apps (like Teams).\n6. In the VPN client's settings, if there's an option to switch the connection type or protocol, try switching it and reconnect.\n\nIf the VPN still drops after trying these steps, please reply with the time of the last three drops, whether you were on Wi-Fi or a cable, and any error message the VPN client showed — that will help us dig further."
        },
        "outcome": "proposed"
      },
