            "KB-011"
          ],
          "confidence": "high",
          "replyMarkdown": "Hi Alex,\n\nSorry about the trouble with the 3rd floor printer. Here's how to fix a printer showing offline:\n\n1. Check the printer itself: make sure it's powered on, has no error shown on its screen, and isn't out of paper or toner.\n2. Check its network connection (cable plugged in, or Wi-Fi shown on its screen). Restart the printer and wait about two minutes.\n3. Make sure your laptop is connected to the office network (or VPN if remote) — printers can't be reached from a home network directly.\n4. On Windows: go to Settings > Printers and scanners, select the printer, open **Printer properties**, and make sure **Use printer offline** is not ticked.\n   On a Mac: remove the printer and add it again.\n5. Restart your laptop and try printing a test page.\n\nIf it still shows offline afterwards, or if print jobs are stuck in the queue, please let us know — and if nobody nearby can print either, mention the printer's name (on a label on the front) and its location so we can look into it further.\n\nThanks,\nIT Service Desk"
        },
        "outcome": "proposed"
