            "KB-024"
          ],
          "confidence": "high",
          "replyMarkdown": "Sorry about the repeated password prompts — this is a common issue right after changing your password, since Outlook (and sometimes your phone) may still be using the old saved password. Here's how to fix it:\n\n1. Close the sign-in box, then close Outlook completely.\n2. Check you can sign in to webmail in a browser with your new password. If that fails too, your password change may not have gone through properly - let us know.\n3. Make sure your laptop has a working internet connection (and is on VPN if you're remote and need it for mail).\n4. Open Outlook again and sign in once. Approve the MFA prompt if asked.\n5. If it still loops, sign out of your work account in your operating system's account settings, restart the laptop, and sign in again.\n6. On Windows, open Credential Manager, remove any saved entries with the mail server or \"Outlook\" in the name, then restart Outlook.\n\nAlso worth checking: if you have your work email set up on your phone, update the password there too, since an old saved password on a phone can also cause this loop.\n\nIf the prompt keeps coming back after trying all of this, please reply with your Outlook version, whether webmail works, and confirm your phone's mail app password is up to date, so we can look further."
        },
        "outcome": "proposed"
      },
