          "confidence": "high",
          "replyMarkdown": "Sorry for the trouble signing in! You can reset your password yourself:\n\n1. On the sign-in page, choose **Forgot password**.\n2. Enter your work email address and approve the verification prompt sent to your registered MFA device.\n3. Choose a new password that meets the rules shown on the page.\n4. Sign in on your laptop with the new password.\n5. Update the saved password on your phone (mail, calendar, Wi-Fi) so it doesn't keep retrying with the old one and lock your account again.\n\nIf it doesn't work:\n- No verification prompt arrives: see the article on MFA prompts not arriving.\n- You no longer have your registered MFA device: see the article on changing/replacing your MFA device.\n- The page says your account is locked: see the article on accounts locked after too many attempts.\n\nNote: the service desk will never ask you for your password directly. If anyone does, please report it instead of replying."
        },
